- MuseCore ClaudeUiControl: the call, the control list (stable ids from SwiftUI accessibility ids/labels), finding a
  control, the refusal list (same as the server's + Claude's own chat box), action mapping, keys; tests
- App MuseUiBridge: reads the app's own accessibility tree in-process (no Accessibility / Screen Recording permission),
  acts on its own controls, menu-bar items and keys; a small JPEG of the MUSE window only (cacheDisplay)
- ClaudeUiOverlay: soft ring on each control Claude touches, "Claude is using MUSE · Esc to stop" pill; Esc stops until
  the person writes again
- Settings → Claude: "Let Claude operate MUSE's screen" (per person, on by default); X-Muse-Caps adds ui
- Identifiers: sidebar (nav.*), title-bar search, Claude's chat box (claude.chat.composer, never operated)

